---
import createBackup from "../../captures/create-backup.png";
import Callout from "../../guide/Callout.astro";
import GuidePage from "../../guide/GuidePage.astro";
import Path from "../../guide/Path.astro";
import PlatformAnswers from "../../guide/PlatformAnswers.astro";
import PlatformLabel from "../../guide/PlatformLabel.astro";
import Task from "../../guide/Task.astro";
import { sitePath } from "../../site/links.ts";
---

<GuidePage manual="docs" slug="backups-and-storage" lead="Katari keeps automatic backups, your own comics and, on Android, downloads in one folder you choose.">
  <Task id="storage-folder" title="The storage folder">
    <p>
      Setup asks for it, and <Path>Settings › Data and storage › Storage location</Path> changes it. Give Katari a folder of its own; it
      fills it like this:
    </p>
    <pre><code>{`Katari/
  autobackup/                      automatic backups
  downloads/                       on Android
    Pepper&Carrot (EN)/            comics, one folder per source
    Blender Studio (EN) [anime]/   video
    Project Gutenberg [book]/      books
  local/                           your own comics`}</code></pre>
    <p>
      <PlatformLabel platform="Android" lead />Inside <code>downloads/</code>, each title has a folder of its own. After moving or deleting
      files there yourself, tap <Path>Settings › Advanced › Reindex downloads</Path> so Katari notices.
    </p>
  </Task>

  <Task id="backup" title="Back up" shot={{ image: createBackup, alt: "What a backup can keep, each with a box to tick", caption: "Create backup" }}>
    <ol>
      <li>Open <Path>Settings › Data and storage</Path> and select <strong>Create backup</strong>.</li>
      <li>
        Tick what to keep: library entries, chapters, tracking, history, categories, all read entries, app settings, extension stores and
        source settings.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Include sensitive settings (e.g., tracker login tokens)</strong> adds logins and other private settings. Keep a backup with
        them somewhere only you can reach.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      With more than one profile, the screen also lists them, all ticked. Untick the ones to leave out. Locked ones ask to be unlocked
      when you select <strong>Create</strong>.
    </p>
  </Task>

  <Task id="automatic" title="Automatic backups">
    <p>
      Katari backs up every profile by itself every 12 hours and keeps the last four in <code>autobackup/</code>. Change how often under
      <strong>Automatic backup frequency</strong>.
    </p>
    <PlatformAnswers>
      <p slot="android">Backups run in the background, also while Katari is closed.</p>
      <p slot="linux">Backups run while Katari is open. One missed while it was closed runs when Katari next starts.</p>
    </PlatformAnswers>
    <p>
      Each app names its backups after itself, so they can share one folder: <code>katari_2026-10-13_09-30.tachibk</code> from Katari,
      <code>katari.foss_…</code> from Katari FOSS and <code>katari.desktop_…</code> from Katari for Linux.
    </p>
    <Callout label="No logins">
      <p>Automatic backups never include sensitive settings. After restoring one, log in to your trackers again.</p>
    </Callout>
  </Task>

  <Task id="left-out" title="What a backup leaves out">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Left out</th> <th>After a restore</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><PlatformLabel platform="Android" lead /><strong>Downloads</strong></td> <td>Keep the storage folder, or download again</td></tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Extensions and their trust</strong></td>
          <td>Install them again. Ones that didn't come from a restored extension store need trusting again</td>
        </tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Translation servers and API keys</strong></td> <td>Enter them again</td></tr>
        <tr><td><PlatformLabel platform="Android" lead /><strong>Text recognition models</strong></td> <td>Katari offers to download them again when a page needs them</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Sensitive settings</strong>, unless ticked</td> <td>Log in to trackers and sources again</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </Task>

  <Task id="restore" title="Restore">
    <ol>
      <li>Select <strong>Restore backup</strong> in <Path>Settings › Data and storage</Path>, or in setup, and pick the <code>.tachibk</code> file.</li>
      <li>Choose what to bring back: library, categories, app settings, extension stores, source settings.</li>
      <li>
        If the backup holds several profiles, untick the ones to skip. Each one is either added as a new profile or merges into the profile
        it came from, and locked ones ask to be unlocked first.
      </li>
      <li>Katari then lists missing sources and trackers you aren't logged into. Install those extensions and log in.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Restoring doesn't switch the profile you're using. Backups from Mihon and Tachiyomi restore the same way. Old JSON backups don't.</p>
  </Task>

  <Task id="mihon" title="Move from Mihon">
    <p>
      Backups from Mihon restore like Katari's own. <a href={sitePath("docs/coming-from-mihon/")}>Coming from Mihon</a> covers the whole
      move, extensions included, and on Android downloads too.
    </p>
  </Task>
</GuidePage>
